SUMMARY:Bunker Drama Thriller at TIFF 2026 + Lunch (Princess of Wales)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**On Tuesday September 15th\,** **see Bunk
 er at the 51st edition of the Toronto International Film Festival (TIFF)**
 . Oscar winners Penélope Cruz and Javier Bardem play a couple whose bond 
 is tested when a mysterious billionaire’s proposal prompts an ethical im
 passe in the latest from Oscar-winning writer-director Florian Zeller (TIF
 F ’20’s *The Father*). When a mysterious billionaire asks Miguel (Bard
 em) to design a luxury bunker where a tiny cluster of the ultra-wealthy ca
 n take shelter in an apocalypse\, the offer appeals to his vanity as much 
 as his pocketbook - an opportunity to furnish a pyramid for a modern-day p
 haraoh. But for Sofia (Cruz)\, the proposal reeks of the gross inequality 
 that is destroying the world. Bardem and Cruz infuse their roles with comp
 lexity and vulnerability in this tale of affluence\, paranoia\, and ambiti
 on\, where there is nothing more precious than love.... i am in Orchestra 
 Q39. **Purchase Bunker on Tuesday September 15th at 11am. There are three 
 extra tickets (seated with others) available for purchase\; message me if 
 you're interested.**\n\n**COST**\nRegular Cost: $35.73 - $42.51 includes t
 axes and fees\n\nExtra tickets: $35.73 and $38.50\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee:
  $5\n\n**Ticket Policy**: All sales are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n
 \n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes confirming if you will join for lunch aft
 er. (Everyone goes on the waitlist until they post their seat number or st
 ate they will be doing Rush.)**\n* **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.c
 a/event/1000650B16C63801)** **your own ticket for Tuesday\, September 15th
  at 11am**\, post your seat number and I will move you to going. Note: tic
 kets are currently showing as sold out\, but that can change at any time a
 s they release more tickets or people make exchanges.\n* Alternately\, you
  can message me for the extra tickets\, and it will be confirmed once paym
 ent is received by etransfer. Ticket will be provided at the event start t
 ime.\n* Rush is also possible\, requiring you to line up 1 hour before sho
 wtime. 15 mins prior to start time\, an attendance check is completed and 
 any available seats are sold at regular price + $2\n\nA reminder will be s
 ent the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and whe
 n.\n\nRSVPs close 2 days prior. Cancellations will result in a No Show and
  impact future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for the Show at: 
 10:30am inside the Princess of Wales Theatre at 300 King St. W**\, **on th
 e ground floor** **to the right side of the box office after scanning your
  tickets.**\n\n**Start: 11am**\n\nLength: 2 hours 6 mins\n\nAfter: meet at
  the initial meeting spot to chat about the show and head out for lunch ne
 ar by.\n\nEnjoy and please post your comments in the Event after.
