SUMMARY:World Premiere Ink based on a true story (TIFF 2026) + Dinner -Pri
 ncess of Wales
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\nNote: This is a premium performance.\n\n**
 On Tuesday September 15th\,** **see Ink at the 51st edition of the Toronto
  International Film Festival (TIFF)\, my second choice for movies after Fj
 ord**. Fast-paced and gripping\, Boyle’s *Ink* traces the dark journalis
 tic legacy of *The Sun* that continues to reverberate today. Director Dann
 y Boyle (TIFF ’08’s People Choice Award winner *Slumdog Millionaire*) 
 stylishly adapts playwright James Graham’s wild recounting of how *The S
 un* became one of the most successful newspapers in British history while 
 launching tabloid culture. I am in Dress Circle Seat D38. **Purchase Ink o
 n Tuesday September 15th at 2:30pm.**\n\nRupert Murdoch (Guy Pearce\, *The
  Brutalist*\, TIFF ’24) persuades newspaper editor Larry Lamb (Jack O’
 Connell) to oversee his newly acquired but flagging daily\, *The Sun*. But
  how to grab readers in the highly competitive British media market? Be ex
 treme\, throwing anything onto the page that will make a splash\, the more
  titillating\, the better. The tactic works\, and soon the notorious *Sun*
  sees a massive spike in circulation.\n\nThe goal of casting a wide net fo
 r new readers creates just enough space for one woman (Claire Foy) to brea
 k through and pitch articles with a modern woman’s perspective. It’s n
 ot long before she starts to brush against the limits of the prevailing bo
 ys’ club culture within the industry. And as readership numbers rise\, s
 o do the paper’s detractors.\n\n**COST**\nRegular Cost: $98 + fees\n\nMe
 etup Organizer Fee: $5\n\n**Ticket Policy**: All sales are final\, no refu
 nds or exchanges.\n\n**SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes (Everyone goes on the 
 waitlist until they post their seat number or state they will be doing Rus
 h.)**\n* **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/event/1000650B16C93807)*
 * **your own ticket for Tuesday\, September 15th at 2:30pm**\, post your s
 eat number and I will move you to going. Note: tickets are still available
  at time of posting\, and I have had 8 opportunities to buy tickets to-dat
 e\, so keep trying if it says currently sold out.\n* Rush is also possible
 \, requiring you to line up 1 hour before showtime. 15 mins prior to start
  time\, an attendance check is completed and any available seats are sold 
 at regular price + $2\n\nA reminder will be sent the day before with my ce
 ll and reminder details where to meet and when.\n\nRSVPs close 2 days prio
 r. Cancellations will result in a No Show and impact future attendance.\n\
 n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me for the Show at: 2pm inside the Princess of Wa
 les Theatre at 300 King St. W**\, **on the ground floor** **to the right s
 ide of the box office after scanning your tickets.**\n\n**Start: 2:30pm**\
 n\nLength: 1 hour 56 mins\n\nAfter: we're heading out right after for dinn
 er and can talk along the way.\n\nAfter: meet at the initial meeting spot 
 to chat about the show and head out.\n\nEnjoy and please post your comment
 s in the Event after.
