SUMMARY:Being Heumann True Story Drama at TIFF 2026 + Dinner (TIFF Lightbo
 x)
DESCRIPTION:Experience Toronto\n**On Saturday September 19th\,** join me t
 o **see Being Heumann at the 51st edition of the Toronto International Fil
 m Festival (TIFF)**. *Heumann* is the opening and closing show for TIFF 20
 26. Featuring a breakout performance by Ruth Madeley and Oscar nominee Mar
 k Ruffalo\, this inspiring historical drama from Oscar-winning filmmaker S
 iân Heder (*CODA*) celebrates the paradigm-shifting activist Judy Heumann
 \, “Mother of the Disability Rights Movement.” Every bit as moving as 
 her Best Picture Oscar winner\, *CODA*\, *Heumann* tells the remarkable tr
 ue story of the woman who led a world-changing campaign for accessibility.
  Judy Heumann rallied a handful\, then dozens\, then hundreds of ordinary 
 Americans with disabilities to push the US government to live up to its co
 mmitments. Though set in the past\, *Being Heumann* couldn’t be more per
 tinent to our present. When change can seem overwhelming\, we need heroes 
 like Judy to galvanize us. My seat is Balcony BB13. **Purchase Being Heuma
 nn on Saturday September 19th at 6pm. There is one extra ticket (seated to
 gether) available for purchase\; message me if you're interested.**\n\n**C
 OST**\nRegular Cost: $38.73 includes all fees\n\nMeetup Organizer Fee: $5\
 n\n**Ticket Policy**: All sales are final\, no refunds or exchanges.\n\n**
 SIGNING-UP**\n\n* **RSVP Yes confirming if you will join for dinner after.
  (Everyone goes on the waitlist until they post their seat number or state
  they will be doing Rush.)**\n* **[Purchase](https://www.ticketmaster.ca/e
 vent/1000650B07682680)** **your own ticket for Saturday\, September 19th a
 t 6pm**\, post your seat number and I will move you to going. Note: ticket
 s are currently showing as sold out\, but that can change at any time as t
 hey release more tickets or people make exchanges.\n* Alternately\, you ca
 n message me for the extra ticket\, and it will be confirmed once payment 
 is received by etransfer. Ticket will be provided at the event start time.
 \n* Rush is also possible\, requiring you to line up 1 hour before showtim
 e. 15 mins prior to start time\, an attendance check is completed and any 
 available seats are sold at regular price + $2\n\nA reminder will be sent 
 the day before with my cell and reminder details where to meet and when.\n
 \nRSVPs close 1 day prior. Cancellations will result in a No Show and impa
 ct future attendance.\n\n**MEETUP TIME**\n**Meet me at: 5:30pm inside TIFF
  Lightbox at 350 King St. W**\, **on the ground floor** **to the right sid
 e of the box office after scanning your tickets.**\n\n**Start: 6pm**\n\nLe
 ngth: 2 hours 7 mins\n\nAfter: meet outside the auditorium to chat about t
 he show and head out for dinner near by.\n\nEnjoy and please post your com
 ments in the Event after.
